Z||000000||Jaei Sun||09-25-2001||12:27 PM||||I had my roof skin removed when I had my car painted and the "black tar" like ooze that is between the SMC skin and the metal frame was removed and tossed.  Now I need to reapply this stuff before I put the roof back together.  Can I get this stuff from an autoparts store or do I have to go to GM and spend probably more $$ than I want to on theirs??<P>If I go the GM route does anyone have the part # of this stuff or even know what it's called??  <P>Thanks a ton to anyone who replys!!!!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-25-2001||12:36 PM||||How'd the repaint go? I guess we should be seeing you back on the road shortly- yes?  As for the "Tar" stuff, I believe I've heard people suggest getting something like silicone sealer (preferably not a permanant one... you'll never remove the roof again if you do that!)  Sorry I couldn't be more specific. When are you going to be back on the road?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
