Z||000008||theogre||09-25-2001||07:49 PM||||Far as I know it's the same adhesive used for mounting the windshield. You can get it fairly easy thru most parts stores.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||rockcrawl||09-25-2001||07:52 PM||||Yes, you are looking for butyl rubber. It comes on a roll usually packaged in a flat square box. It is available in different sizes. It is commonly used to install windows...it's the same stuff that holds the rear window in the Fiero. It's available at any good auto parts store. Most modern cars use Urethane to hold the windshield in. That's the stuff that comes in a tube like caulk, It sets up firm so it would make future removal of the panel almost impossible without damage.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||09-25-2001||09:07 PM||||Butyl rubber on a roll?!<BR>I wish I woulda known that. <BR>The stuff that I bought <I>was</I> butyl rubber in a tube, and it was very thin. PITA to work with. <BR>I hope Ronnie never has to remove those moldings, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Jimmy||09-25-2001||10:16 PM||||Yeah, when I swapped in a sunroof on my 84 SE I used the butyl on a roll.<P>Jim||||reg||1
